--- pytest-asyncio 1.4.0 changelog evidence (Amendment ii · verbatim) ---
Source: https://pytest-asyncio.readthedocs.io/en/v1.4.0/reference/changelog.html
Direct-match items to `RuntimeError: Event loop is closed` teardown-leak class:

  1. `loop.shutdown_asyncgens` now called before closing the event loop —
     async-generator cleanup consistent with `asyncio.run` behavior.
  2. Internal changes to prevent errors during the cleanup of async generators
     if the event loop has already been closed. ← direct match for our failure
     class.
  3. Explicit cleanup of stale event loops during setup/teardown of the
     `event_loop` fixture — teardown-leak class fix.
  4. New `pytest_asyncio_loop_factories` hook (deprecates `event_loop_policy`
     fixture) — sync `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` functions correctly identify
     the event loop even when test code disrupts current loop via
     `asyncio.run` / `asyncio.set_event_loop(None)`. Potential Path-2 lever.
  5. Fix for `ResourceWarning: unclosed event loop` when sync test calls
     `asyncio.run` or otherwise manually unsets the event loop after plugin
     has executed an async test or fixture.

